{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 779 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fc20a279ceec417c6182f1cc1002a0cf36f47501dbc83a90bd091fb06f42cadd" :edb/db-before-t 778 :edb/db-after-t 779 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534091 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:50:49.335Z" 13194139534091 true] [17592186054522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277313 13194139534091 true] [17592186054616 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277303 13194139534091 true] [17592186059717 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277290 13194139534091 true] [17592186068688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277283 13194139534091 true] [17592186073754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277327 13194139534091 true] [17592186079101 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534091 true] [17592186079101 1100 "Factor the expression $p^{4} - 1$." 13194139534091 false] [17592186079101 1100 "Factor the expression ${p}^{4}-1.$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186079101 1145 "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{p}^{4}-1={({p}^{2})}^{2}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({p}^{2})}^{2}-{1}^{2}=({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-1)\n$$\n\nFinally, we notice that the expression in the second set of parentheses is also a difference of squares. Therefore, the expression can be factored further, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-1) & =({p}^{2}+1)({p}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =({p}^{2}+1)(p+1)(p-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186083147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277276 13194139534091 true] [17592186087708 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277320 13194139534091 true] [17592186087767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277306 13194139534091 true] [17592186259310 1017 #edb/ref 17592186274611 13194139534091 false] [17592186259310 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277297 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277277 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1089 "q-112964" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1100 "For the polynomial $f(x)=20{x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}+x-4,$ how many *potential* roots are given by the rational roots theorem?" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1113 #uuid "eb95820b-48e7-589b-b453-db9d5d27848d" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277276 1145 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $-4,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2$ and $\\pm 4.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $20,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2,$ $\\pm 4,$ $\\pm 5,$ $\\pm 10$ and $\\pm 20.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{20}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{20}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{4}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{4}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to the lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{20}, \\\\ \\pm 2, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{10}, \\\\ \\pm 4, & \\pm 2, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{4}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{5}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that several potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{20},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{10},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{5},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{2}{5},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{4}{5},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $20$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 10=20.$)" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277278 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277279 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277280 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277281 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277282 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1041 "selection" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277279 13194139534091 true] [17592186277277 1110 #uuid "76db370d-a620-5984-a449-0cfdc8dc982b" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277278 1034 "12" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277278 1111 #uuid "29d1479d-8b8d-5bbb-bb1d-3e4a244cb137" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277279 1034 "20" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277279 1111 #uuid "fcf4139c-b2ca-5302-89d4-ab02d05b733f" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277280 1034 "16" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277280 1111 #uuid "3e82a6db-a670-5b09-bb4d-afd3cb9f40be" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277281 1034 "36" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277281 1111 #uuid "bea7083f-5aaa-5edd-9dee-9e0640acf362" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277282 1034 "32" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277282 1111 #uuid "90efd263-4e21-5a4c-be10-bd1febf0ea78" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277284 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1089 "q-113824" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1100 "Given that $\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}=a$ and $\\frac{12g}{7h}=b,$ what is $a÷b?$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1113 #uuid "6a48aa76-c7fd-50b2-ab17-7f90486ab6d7" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277283 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\na÷b=\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}÷\\frac{12g}{7h},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}÷\\frac{12g}{7h} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{g}^{2}}{7{h}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{12g} & = \\\\ \\frac{4g\\cdot g}{7h\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{7h}{3\\cdot 4g} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4g}\\cdot g}{\\cancel{7h}\\cdot {h}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{7h}}{3\\cdot \\cancel{4g}} & = \\\\ \\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277285 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277286 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277287 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277288 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277289 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1041 "selection" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277285 13194139534091 true] [17592186277284 1110 #uuid "ecc0b8cc-ff19-5dab-aa5c-9928ba09585b" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277285 1034 "\\frac{g}{3{h}^{2}}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277285 1111 #uuid "5852f3fa-1509-517d-918f-e9399357ea6c" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277286 1034 "\\frac{{g}^{2}}{3h}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277286 1111 #uuid "b79330e2-2190-5dde-807b-d4dd36d62d9e" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277287 1034 "\\frac{3{h}^{2}}{g}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277287 1111 #uuid "a2aa00d6-1cf0-511d-b817-de62406915cf" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277288 1034 "\\frac{g{h}^{2}}{3}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277288 1111 #uuid "e3758285-9f52-5c48-83a2-1eba067b94e3" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277289 1034 "\\frac{3g}{{h}^{2}}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277289 1111 #uuid "dd121968-abe1-58d1-baf3-51275f7e9f2b" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277291 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1089 "q-122084" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1100 "Linda wants to buy a refreshing drink. The store has $6$ types of sodas, $6$ types of juices, and $3$ types of water. How many choices of drinks does Linda have?" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1113 #uuid "ad69f963-f40c-56bd-95d6-2dfbeeffb73d" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277290 1145 "In order to find the total number of choices Linda has, we can use the **rule of sum**:\n\n$$\n6+6+3=15\n$$\n\nTherefore, Linda has $15$ choices of drinks." 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277292 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277293 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277294 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277295 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277296 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1041 "selection" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277295 13194139534091 true] [17592186277291 1110 #uuid "27c4f0b8-3764-5138-ba84-e50d86d49c0e" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277292 1034 "12" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277292 1111 #uuid "ae07c290-23e0-52d1-95c9-b380b57d031a" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277293 1034 "9" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277293 1111 #uuid "b31136a5-eaf4-5204-ad5d-af3ae64355bf" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277294 1034 "3" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277294 1111 #uuid "3ef6b23f-604f-5240-8d10-c59c2a0cb082" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277295 1034 "15" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277295 1111 #uuid "2b590086-e3b7-5da3-87b0-d6206eb0052e" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277296 1034 "6" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277296 1111 #uuid "850e4ac8-2c5a-5363-b704-e476ae06ea6e" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277298 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277299 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277300 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277301 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277302 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1041 "selection" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277302 13194139534091 true] [17592186277297 1110 #uuid "b3d1e849-3022-5eb8-93a3-6a5fe5ac7a52" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277298 1034 "\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277298 1111 #uuid "0fbed6fe-e67e-519e-8d16-d23e07b37b0b" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277299 1034 "-\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277299 1111 #uuid "970c727b-5391-5e23-8e4f-b5762579af66" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277300 1034 "2" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277300 1111 #uuid "0efafccd-3dbf-5c2d-a483-35b87103e117" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277301 1034 "\\frac{5}{7}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277301 1111 #uuid "f9a7cf08-da54-5f93-915f-037a866067b9" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277302 1034 "-2" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277302 1111 #uuid "2c1e3f06-2e8a-5995-a897-4290e1b746d0" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277304 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1089 "q-338378" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/assets/601562e6fab230b818a1776e42b700518f803f425dcb7f407d3659e91db0ff33.png)\n\nIf the figure above shows the graph of $f(x),$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1113 #uuid "4a7fff84-7ff5-5fce-a049-e02df71c9444" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277303 1145 "Using the power and quotient rules, we can rewrite the given limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2))}^{2}}{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2))}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above is true provided that  ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ exists.\n\nWe find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=1.$ We calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2)=3(1)+2=5\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2)=1-2=-1\n$$\n\nSo we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{25}{-1}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277305 13194139534091 true] [17592186277304 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534091 true] [17592186277304 1041 "field-1" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277304 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277305 13194139534091 true] [17592186277304 1110 #uuid "4e728ba8-2a52-51e7-8d74-28dc61c5396a" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277305 1034 "-25" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277305 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277305 1111 #uuid "9fcd4b38-1446-5ae3-97ad-552f58e65adb" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277307 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1089 "q-66428" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1100 "Solve  the equation $\\,-{x}^{2}-2x-17=0.$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1113 #uuid "79f12e46-deae-53cd-89d3-2dfcd47a8848" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277306 1145 "We can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=-1,b=-2,$ and $c=-17.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(-1)(-17)}}{2(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{4-68}}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-64}}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}}{-2} \\\\  & =-1\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-1+4\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-1-4\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277308 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277309 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277310 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277311 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277312 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1041 "selection" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277308 13194139534091 true] [17592186277307 1110 #uuid "a3c23881-8e59-5522-abe3-28fec3edc201" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277308 1034 "x=-1\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277308 1111 #uuid "457e804b-10aa-59ee-88ad-3a839f73934f" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277309 1034 "x=-2\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277309 1111 #uuid "feaefaee-d395-5bc6-920a-c159d21b355e" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277310 1034 "x=-1\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277310 1111 #uuid "f33946c4-048f-5adf-8e5e-b5aa8bc2392c" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277311 1034 "x=-2\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277311 1111 #uuid "785de841-e30d-5554-ae18-9a5bcd989d09" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277312 1034 "x=-1\\pm \\,\\text{i}" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534091 true] [17592186277312 1111 #uuid "f7dbe447-f2c7-5e0d-bdb3-f03c81cfa689" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277314 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1089 "q-71164" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1113 #uuid "820f101a-d00c-5982-8568-97f2eedadddf" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277313 1145 "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277315 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277316 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277317 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277318 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277319 13194139534091 true] [17592186277314 1